    "body": "Adds four Debug sidebar sections \u2014 **Evaluation**, **Statics**, **Editor &\nMemory**, **Frame Timing** \u2014 showing where a keystroke's time goes and what the\neditor currently holds. They share a table, a formatter and a heat map with\n#2370's **Worker Messaging** panel, which moves onto the same pieces.\n\n## Up front: refs and side effects, deliberately\n\nThe collectors are module-level refs, written by side-effecting calls at the\npoints being measured rather than values threaded through the component tree.\nDeliberately: this is developer instrumentation \u2014 tangential to the codebase, off\na normal user's path, inert unless a panel is open \u2014 and doing it properly would\nmean widening every `update` / `calculate` signature along the way to carry a\nvalue only a debug panel reads. Worth revisiting if these panels ever become\nload-bearing.\n\nWhat a section touches is still closed: each collector and `PerfFormat` has a\n`.rei`, each section is pinned to `DebugSection.S`, and the mutation stays inside\nthe collectors.\n\n## What gets collected\n\n**Stage timings, per keystroke.** The edit action's `perform` (update phase), then\neach calculate-phase stage \u2014 statics + elaboration, the syntax-cache rebuild\n(MakeTerm + Measured), cursor info, the ExplainThis color map \u2014 and the total. 30\nframes kept; a stage that didn't run shows `\u2014`, never a misleading `0`.\n\n**The eval round trip, per request.** The latency the main thread sees\n(`postMessage` \u2192 `onmessage`) beside the worker's own evaluator time, which it now\nreturns in a new `eval_time` on `ServerMessage.result` \u2014 so the gap between them\nis queue + serialization + transfer. Plus the outcome, encoded payload sizes and a\nrestart count. 10 requests kept.\n\n**Structural counts, per frame.** Info-map entries, error and warning counts, why\nstatics ran or didn't (recomputed / forced / deferred / cached), segment tokens,\ntiles, rows, projectors, and live undo/redo/backpack depth.\n\nDurations are `Core.Time_ns.Span`, sizes `Core.Byte_units`. Byte-exact heap sizes\nare deliberately absent \u2014 walking the heap per frame is too expensive, and timings\nplus counts answer the question.\n\n## The changes, in reading order\n\n1. **`util/Metrics.re`** (new) \u2014 the gate and bounded history every collector\n   shares, as a functor; recorders run through `when_enabled`. Read first.\n2. **`util/PerfMetrics.re`** \u2014 per-frame collector: the `frame` record, the\n   `time_*` stage wrappers, the count recorders.\n3. **`util/EvalMetrics.re`** \u2014 round-trip collector, keyed by request id so its\n   rows line up with Worker Messaging's.\n4. **`util/WorkerMetrics.re`** \u2014 pre-existing; moved onto the functor.\n5. **`CodeEditable`, `CodeWithStatics`, `Page`, `History`** \u2014 where the timings\n   are taken, and where gating syncs once per cycle.\n6. **`util/WorkerServer.re`, `util/WorkerClient.re`** \u2014 evaluator time on the\n   wire, and the recording around the request lifecycle.\n7. **`sidebar/PerfFormat.re`** \u2014 the table vocabulary: a `column` carries header,\n   tooltip and cell projection; `cell` is opaque; `view` assembles a body.\n8. **`sidebar/*Section.re`** \u2014 one per panel: columns plus a `view` call.\n9. **`sidebar/SidebarModel.re`, `Settings.re`** \u2014 sidebar settings store\n   `debug_expanded`, so the whole Debug sidebar starts collapsed.\n10. **`util/TimeUtil.re`** \u2014 `timed`, and the `span` alias that lets a deriving\n    type carry a `Time_ns.Span`. The only file outside `src/web/`.\n\n## Closed panels cost nothing\n\nEach collector is gated on **its own** section being expanded, synced once per\ncycle in `Page.Update.calculate`, and every section ships collapsed \u2014 so ordinary\nediting pays nothing.\n\n## Testing\n\n`make dev` clean, `make test-quick` green (3311), and a manual pass over all five\nsections in Chrome. `Test_WorkerServer` covers a `Time_ns.Span` surviving Marshal\n+ `structuredClone` and its nanosecond json encoding.\n",
